# Bejeweled Warg, cast on turn 1 off a Mox, connects on turn 3 and Bot1 chooses the Treasure mode as the trigger goes on
# the stack. On turn 5 it connects again and Bot1 chooses the counter mode: the Warg is the only Wolf Bot1 controls, so
# its target is not asked. Bot1 then cracks the Treasure for red, the only red it has, to Bolt Bot2.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Mox Emerald
Bejeweled Warg
Lightning Bolt
Forest x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x14

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Bejeweled Warg.Cast
Bot1.Attack(Bejeweled Warg)
Bot1.Modes(Create a Treasure token)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot1.Battlefield = Forest; Mox Emerald; Bejeweled Warg; Treasure Token
? Bot2.Life = 17
Bot1.Attack(Bejeweled Warg)
Bot1.Modes(Put a +1/+1 counter)
Bot1.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot2)
Bot1.Battlefield.Treasure Token.Activate(Color: Red)

[Expect]
Turn = 5
Bot1.Battlefield = Forest; Mox Emerald; Bejeweled Warg
Bot1.Battlefield.Bejeweled Warg.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Bejeweled Warg.Power = 4
Bot1.Graveyard = Lightning Bolt
Bot2.Life = 11
